# ==============================================================================
# What does not reach the build context
# ==============================================================================
# Docker takes a directory whole: `COPY ./src ./src/` brings along what git
# does not track. That is how `src/link_shortener.egg-info`, left behind by
# installing the package into the working tree, rode into the image. It
# declared version 0.1.0 and shadowed the installed package's metadata,
# because `/app/src` precedes site-packages on `sys.path`: in the container
# `importlib.metadata.version("link-shortener")` answered 0.1.0 while the
# correct `link_shortener-0.9.0.dist-info` sat right beside it.
#
# Patterns are matched from the context root, and `*` does not cross a `/`:
# `*.egg-info` would not have covered `src/link_shortener.egg-info` -- hence
# the `**/`.
#
# The second consequence is size: without this file the whole tree was sent
# to the daemon, `.venv` and `.git` included.
# ==============================================================================

# Artefacts of installing and building
**/*.egg-info
**/__pycache__
**/*.py[oc]
build/
dist/
wheels/

# Environments and tool caches
.venv/
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/

# The repository and its settings
.git/
.gitignore
.github/

# Reports left by runs
htmlcov/
coverage.xml
.coverage
test-results/

# Settings carrying secrets: they are not copied into the image, and have
# no business in the context either
.env
.env.*

# Everything a run leaves behind: databases and journals
datas/

# Not copied by the Dockerfile. The `dockers/` directory stays: that is
# where `entrypoint.sh` comes from
tests/
docs/

# Rubbish from the OS and from editors
**/.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/
